{% comment %}
  CartBloom app embed.

  An *embed* block (target: body), not an app block. Cart-drawer sections do not
  accept @app blocks, so the widget cannot be placed by the merchant there — it
  loads globally and mounts itself into the drawer. The cart *page* gets a real
  app block separately, where drag-and-drop placement does work.

  This file exists to do exactly one thing beyond loading assets: inline the
  offer config from the shop metafield. That is what keeps the storefront off
  our infrastructure entirely — no app proxy, no fetch, no latency, and no
  hosting cost that scales with a merchant's traffic (spec §4).

  If the metafield is missing or storefront access was never granted on its
  definition, `cfg` is nil and nothing renders. That is deliberate: a widget
  that renders a progress bar it cannot compute would show a wrong number.
{% endcomment %}

{%- comment -%}
  The reserved prefix is the bracketed string "$app", not a dot-path segment.

  `shop.metafields.app.…` looks plausible and is silently wrong: Liquid reads
  `app` as a literal namespace name, finds nothing (the real namespace is
  `app--<app_id>`), and yields an empty object. The widget then renders nothing
  on a store where both the metafield and its definition are perfectly correct
  — no error, no warning, nothing in the console.

  "$app" is the portable alias for `app--<app_id>`, so this survives moving
  between development and production apps without hardcoding an ID.

  https://shopify.dev/docs/apps/build/online-store/theme-app-extensions/configuration
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign cfg = shop.metafields["$app"]["cartbloom-widget-config"].value -%}

{% if cfg %}
  <script>
    window.__CARTBLOOM__ = {{ cfg | json }};
    window.__CARTBLOOM__.moneyFormat = {{ shop.money_format | json }};
    window.__CARTBLOOM__.routes = {
      cartAdd: {{ routes.cart_add_url | json }},
      cartChange: {{ routes.cart_change_url | json }},
      cart: {{ routes.cart_url | json }}
    };

    {%- comment -%}
      Placement, configured in the theme editor rather than by editing theme
      code. App Store review treats "paste this snippet into your theme" as a
      failure regardless of how small the snippet is, so the escape hatch for
      themes our heuristics get wrong lives here, as a setting a merchant fills
      in from the editor.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    window.__CARTBLOOM__.placement = {
      selector: {{ block.settings.placement_selector | default: '' | json }},
      position: {{ block.settings.placement_position | default: 'after' | json }}
    };
  </script>

  {{ 'cartbloom.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
  <script src="{{ 'cartbloom.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{% else %}
  {%- comment -%}
    Deliberately visible in view-source. "Nothing rendered" is otherwise
    indistinguishable from "the embed is not enabled", and that ambiguity cost
    real time to diagnose once already.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <!-- CartBloom: embed active, but shop metafield app/cartbloom-widget-config is empty or unreadable -->
{% endif %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "CartBloom progress bar",
  "target": "body",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Placement"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "CartBloom finds your cart drawer on its own in most themes. If the bar appears somewhere unexpected, name the element it should attach to and CartBloom will use that instead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "placement_selector",
      "label": "Attach to element",
      "info": "A CSS selector, for example .drawer__header or #CartDrawer .cart-items. Leave empty to place it automatically."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "placement_position",
      "label": "Position",
      "options": [
        { "value": "after", "label": "Below that element" },
        { "value": "before", "label": "Above that element" },
        { "value": "prepend", "label": "Inside it, at the top" },
        { "value": "append", "label": "Inside it, at the bottom" }
      ],
      "default": "after"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
